Title      : cpu_cop0: exception address written one cycle later from registers
Project    : fpga-mister (patch for N64_MiSTer 5725381)
Author     : Konstantin Schmidt (mr_pleasant@gmx.de)
Company    : OHRZ
Created    : 2026-10-31
Description:
  On an address error or TLB exception COP0 writes the faulting address to
  BadVAddr, EntryHi (VPN, region), Context BadVPN and XContext.  The write
  enable comes from exception3 (exceptionNew3 of cpu.vhd, combinational from
  the memory address adder) and fans out to ~250 flip-flops; with the address
  mux behind it these were ~190 of the failing CPU endpoints at 93.75 MHz on
  the xc7z020 (BadVAddr -1.350 ns after patch 0001).
  The address (from registers and exceptionNewPC only: the select by
  exception3 matters only with the write enable set, where the order of the
  TLB selects gives the same value) and the enable are now registered and
  written at the start of the next ce cycle, before every other write of the
  process, so MTC0, TLBR and a new exception still win as before; a TLBR in
  the same cycle as the exception (which won in the original) cancels the
  pending EntryHi part.  Every reader of these fields (readValue, the TLBP
  compare, the TLBWI/TLBWR write data, cop0_export) sees the pending value,
  so all outputs are the same in every cycle for any input sequence.  Bench
  n64_cop0_diff_tb (original against patched entity, all outputs and all
  exported COP0 registers twice per cycle, random stimulus without pipeline
  rules).
--- a/rtl/cpu_cop0.vhd	2026-10-31 19:28:54.859249399 +0100
+++ b/rtl/cpu_cop0.vhd	2026-10-31 19:28:54.867263185 +0100
@@ -169,6 +169,18 @@
    signal COP0_20_XCONTEXT_PTE            : unsigned(30 downto 0) := (others => '0');
    signal COP0_20_XCONTEXT_Region         : unsigned(1 downto 0) := (others => '0');
    signal COP0_20_XCONTEXT_BadVPN         : unsigned(26 downto 0) := (others => '0');
